        "question": {
          ":question/id": "33200626-95bd-52f1-9b01-bf2f87144bb2",
          ":question/problem": "The row echelon form matrix $A$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 8 & 6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $A$ has $3$ pivots in the $2$nd, $3$rd, and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 8 & 6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $1$st column.",
